A run that fails - the model crashed or timed out, or produced no
simulated equivalent for some observation - writes \strong{no output file at
all}, and that is deliberate. PEST++ has its own mechanism for this:
PANTHER marks the run failed, retries it up to \code{max_run_fail} times, and
\code{EnsembleMethod} then drops that realisation from the parameter and
observation ensembles. Verified against pestpp-ies 5.2.16: of six
