cannot tell a sentinel from a simulated value, so \code{999} does not mean
"this run failed", it means "the model simulated 999 degrees here". The
realisation then survives into the ensemble statistics and the empirical
covariance that computes the parameter update, until some \code{ies_bad_phi}
threshold happens to catch it - and both of those thresholds are
disabled by default.

The run is still recorded in the run log with \code{na_value}, so it reaches
the results database as \code{NA} and stays visible as a failure, exactly as
